  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `chipDiscovery.ts` to confirm the exact chip-derivation rules (attribute-type → chip-type mapping; the layoutXml column requirement) and `DataGridConfiguration.ts` (how config `e1826c4c-…` binds its saved query). Read the shipped config record's as-built notes (`ai-spaarke-ai-workspace-UI-r2/notes/communications-config-record.md`).</step>
    <step order="2">Inspect the live `sprk_communication` schema + the current bound saved query (view) for config `e1826c4c-9575-f111-ab0e-7ced8ddc4a05` — enumerate which of channel/date/regarding/person columns are already in the view's layoutXml vs missing. Use `dataverse-mcp-usage` / Web API to read the `savedquery`.</step>
    <step order="3">Curate the view's layoutXml to include the target facet columns: `sprk_communicationtype` (channel), `sprk_sentat` (+ `createdon` fallback) (date), the regarding lookups (`sprk_regardingmatter`,… incl. `sprk_regardingperson`), and `sprk_sentby` (person). Keep it the single default view for the config — do NOT create a second.</step>
    <step order="4">Cross-check each curated column against `chipDiscovery.ts`: channel → optionset chip, date → daterange chip, regarding/person → lookup chip. Confirm the attribute types match the expected chip types.</step>
    <step order="5">Deploy the saved-query + config changes via `dataverse-deploy` / Web API; verify (with task 040's page and/or task 030's widget, or via a smoke check) that the intended chips auto-derive and appear. Confirm no second config/view default was created.</step>
    <step order="6">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (041 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (which columns were added to the view, the facet→chip mapping verified against `chipDiscovery.ts`, confirmation of single default config/view, coordination with task 040).</step>
  </steps>

